H7400.definition:
from H7402 (רָכַל)
a scandal-monger (as travelling about)
KJV: slander, carry tales, talebearer.

H7401.definition:
a primitive root;
to soften (intransitively or transitively), used figuratively
KJV: (be) faint(-hearted), mollify, (be, make) soft(-er), be tender.

H7402.definition:
a primitive root;
to travel for trading
KJV: (spice) merchant.

H7403.definition:
from H7402 (רָכַל); merchant;
Rakal, a place in Palestine
KJV: Rachal.

H7404.definition:
feminine passive participle of H7402 (רָכַל);
trade (as peddled)
KJV: merchandise, traffic.

H7405.definition:
a primitive root;
to tie
KJV: bind.

H7406.definition:
from H7405 (רָכַס);
a mountain ridge (as of tied summits)
KJV: rough place.

H7407.definition:
from H7405 (רָכַס);
a snare (as of tied meshes)
KJV: pride.

H7408.definition:
a primitive root;
to lay up, i.e. collect
KJV: gather, get.

H7409.definition:
from H7408 (רָכַשׁ);
a relay of animals on a post-route (as stored up for that purpose); by implication, a courser
KJV: dromedary, mule, swift beast.

H7410.definition:
active participle of H7311 (רוּם); high;
Ram, the name of an Arabian and of an Israelite
KJV: Ram. See also H1027 (בֵּית הָרָם).

H7411.definition:
a primitive root;
to hurl; specifically, to shoot; figuratively, to delude or betray (as if causing to fall)
KJV: beguile, betray, (bow-) man, carry, deceive, throw.

H7412.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7411 (רָמָה);
to throw, set, (figuratively) assess
KJV: cast (down), impose.

H7413.definition:
feminine active participle of H7311 (רוּם);
a height (as a seat of idolatry)
KJV: high place.

H7414.definition:
the same as H7413 (רָמָה);
Ramah, the name of four places in Palestine
KJV: Ramah.

H7415.definition:
from H7426 (רָמַם) in the sense of breeding (compare H7311 (רוּם));
a maggot (as rapidly bred), literally or figuratively
KJV: worm.

H7416.definition:
or רִמֹּן; from H7426 (רָמַם);
a pomegranate, the tree (from its upright growth) or the fruit (also an artificial ornament)
KJV: pomegranate.

H7418.definition:
or רָמַת נֶגֶב; from the plural or construct form of H7413 (רָמָה) and H5045 (נֶגֶב); heights (or height) of the South;
Ramoth-Negeb or Ramath-Negeb, a place in Palestine
KJV: south Ramoth, Ramath of the south.

H7419.definition:
from H7311 (רוּם);
a heap (of carcases)
KJV: height.

H7420.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hurl;
a lance (as thrown); especially the iron point
KJV: buckler, javelin, lancet, spear.

H7421.definition:
for H761 (אֲרַמִּי);
a Ramite, i.e. Aramaean
KJV: Syrian.

H7422.definition:
from H7311 (רוּם) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has raised;
Ramjah, an Israelite
KJV: Ramiah.

H7423.definition:
from H7411 (רָמָה);
remissness, treachery
KJV: deceit(-ful, -fully), false, guile, idle, slack, slothful.

H7424.definition:
of foreign origin;
a brood mare
KJV: dromedary.

H7425.definition:
from an unused root and H3050 (יָהּ) (perhaps meaning to deck); Jah has bedecked;
Remaljah, an Israelite
KJV: Remaliah.

H7426.definition:
a primitive root;
to rise (literally or figuratively)
KJV: exalt, get (oneself) up, lift up (self), mount up.

H7427.definition:
from the active participle of H7426 (רָמַם);
exaltation
KJV: lifting up of self.

H7428.definition:
from H7416 (רִמּוֹן) and H6556 (פֶּרֶץ); pomegranate of the breach;
Rimmon-Perets, a place in the Desert
KJV: Rimmon-parez.

H7429.definition:
a primitive root;
to tread upon (as a potter, in walking or abusively)
KJV: oppressor, stamp upon, trample (under feet), tread (down, upon).

H7430.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to glide swiftly, i.e. to crawl or move with short steps; by analogy to swarm
KJV: creep, move.

H7431.definition:
from H7430 (רָמַשׂ);
a reptile or any other rapidly moving animal
KJV: that creepeth, creeping (moving) thing.

H7432.definition:
from H7411 (רָמָה); height;
Remeth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Remeth.

H7433.definition:
or רָמוֹת גִּלעָד; (2 Chronicles 22:5), from the plural of H7413 (רָמָה) and H1568 (גִּלְעָד); heights of Gilad;
Ramoth-Gilad, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Ramoth-gilead, Ramoth in Gilead. See also H7216 (רָאמוֹת).

H7434.definition:
from H7413 (רָמָה) and H4707 (מִצְפֶּה) with the article interpolated; height of the watch-tower;
Ramath-ham-Mitspeh, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ramath-mizpeh.

H7435.definition:
patronymic of H7414 (רָמָה);
a Ramathite or inhabitant of Ramah
KJV: Ramathite.

H7436.definition:
from the dual of H7413 (רָמָה) and the plural of the active participle of H6822 (צָפָה); double height of watchers;
Ramathajim-Tsophim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ramathaimzophim.

H7437.definition:
from H7413 (רָמָה) and H3895 (לְחִי); height of a jaw-bone;
Ramath-Lechi, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ramath-lehi.

H7438.definition:
from H7442 (רָנַן);
a shout (of deliverance)
KJV: song.

H7439.definition:
a primitive root;
to whiz
KJV: rattle.

H7440.definition:
from H7442 (רָנַן);
properly, a creaking (or shrill sound), i.e. shout (of joy or grief)
KJV: cry, gladness, joy, proclamation, rejoicing, shouting, sing(-ing), triumph.

H7441.definition:
the same as H7440 (רִנָּה);
Rinnah, an Israelite
KJV: Rinnah.

H7442.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to creak (or emit a stridulous sound), i.e. to shout (usually for joy)
KJV: aloud for joy, cry out, be joyful (greatly, make to) rejoice, (cause to) shout (for joy), (cause to) sing (aloud, for joy, out), triumph.

H7443.definition:
from H7442 (רָנַן);
an ostrich (from its wail)
KJV: [idiom] goodly.

H7444.definition:
intensive from H7442 (רָנַן);
shouting (for joy)
KJV: singing.

H7445.definition:
from H7442 (רָנַן);
a shout (for joy)
KJV: joyful (voice), singing, triumphing.

H7446.definition:
from H7450 (רָסַס); a ruin (as dripping to pieces);
Rissah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Rissah.

H7447.definition:
from H7450 (רָסַס);
properly, dripping to pieces, i.e. a ruin; also a dew-drop
KJV: breach, drop.

H7448.definition:
from an unused root meaning to curb;
a halter (as restraining); by implication, the jaw
KJV: bridle.

H7449.definition:
the same as H7448 (רֶסֶן);
Resen, a place in Assyrian
KJV: Resen.

H7451.definition:
from H7489 (רָעַע);
bad or (as noun) evil (natural or moral)
KJV: adversity, affliction, bad, calamity, [phrase] displease(-ure), distress, evil((-favouredness), man, thing), [phrase] exceedingly, [idiom] great, grief(-vous), harm, heavy, hurt(-ful), ill (favoured), [phrase] mark, mischief(-vous), misery, naught(-ty), noisome, [phrase] not please, sad(-ly), sore, sorrow, trouble, vex, wicked(-ly, -ness, one), worse(-st), wretchedness, wrong. (Incl. feminine raaah; as adjective or noun.).

H7452.definition:
from H7321 (רוּעַ);
a crash (of thunder), noise (of war), shout (of joy)
KJV: [idiom] aloud, noise, shouted.

H7453.definition:
or רֵיעַ; from H7462 (רָעָה);
an associate (more or less close)
KJV: brother, companion, fellow, friend, husband, lover, neighbour, [idiom] (an-) other.

H7454.definition:
from H7462 (רָעָה);
a thought (as association of ideas)
KJV: thought.

H7455.definition:
from H7489 (רָעַע);
badness (as marring), physically or morally
KJV: [idiom] be so bad, badness, ([idiom] be so) evil, naughtiness, sadness, sorrow, wickedness.

H7456.definition:
a primitive root;
to hunger
KJV: (suffer to) famish, (be, have, suffer, suffer to) hunger(-ry).

H7457.definition:
from H7456 (רָעֵב);
hungry (more or less intensely)
KJV: hunger bitten, hungry.

H7458.definition:
from H7456 (רָעֵב);
hunger (more or less extensive)
KJV: dearth, famine, [phrase] famished, hunger.

H7460.definition:
a primitive root;
to shudder (more or less violently)
KJV: tremble.

H7461.definition:
or (feminine) רְעָדָהxlit rᵉâdâh corrected to rᵉʻâdâh; from H7460 (רָעַד);
a shudder
KJV: trembling.

H7462.definition:
a primitive root;
to tend a flock; i.e. pasture it; intransitively, to graze (literally or figuratively); generally to rule; by extension, to associate with (as a friend)
KJV: [idiom] break, companion, keep company with, devour, eat up, evil entreat, feed, use as a friend, make friendship with, herdman, keep (sheep) (-er), pastor, [phrase] shearing house, shepherd, wander, waste.

H7463.definition:
from H7462 (רָעָה);
a (male) companion
KJV: friend.

H7464.definition:
feminine of H7453 (רֵעַ);
a female associate
KJV: companion, fellow.

H7465.definition:
for H7455 (רֹעַ);
breakage
KJV: broken, utterly.

H7466.definition:
for H7471 (רְעִי) in the sense of H7453 (רֵעַ); friend;
Reu, a postdiluvian patriarch
KJV: Reu.

H7467.definition:
from the same as H7466 (רְעוּ) and H410 (אֵל); friend of God;
Reuel, the name of Moses' father-in-law, also of an Edomite and an Israelite
KJV: Raguel, Reuel.

H7468.definition:
from H7462 (רָעָה) in the sense of H7453 (רֵעַ);
a female associate; generally an additional one
KJV: [phrase] another, mate, neighbour.

H7469.definition:
probably from H7462 (רָעָה);
a feeding upon, i.e. grasping after
KJV: vexation.

H7470.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7469 (רְעוּת);
desire
KJV: pleasure, will.

H7472.definition:
from H7453 (רֵעַ); social;
Rei, an Israelite
KJV: Rei.

H7473.definition:
from active participle of H7462 (רָעָה);
pastoral; as noun, a shepherd
KJV: shipherd.

H7474.definition:
feminine of H7453 (רֵעַ);
a female associate
KJV: fellow, love.

H7475.definition:
from H7462 (רָעָה) in the sense of H7469 (רְעוּת);
desire
KJV: vexation.

H7476.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7475 (רַעְיוֹן);
a grasp. i.e. (figuratively) mental conception
KJV: cogitation, thought.

H7477.definition:
a primitive root;
to reel, i.e. (figuratively) to brandish
KJV: terribly shake.

H7478.definition:
from H7477 (רָעַל);
a reeling (from intoxication)
KJV: trembling.

H7479.definition:
feminine of H7478 (רַעַל);
a long veil (as fluttering)
KJV: muffler.

H7480.definition:
from H7477 (רָעַל) and H3050 (יָהּ); made to tremble (i.e. fearful) of Jah;
Reelajah, an Israelite
KJV: Reeliah.

H7481.definition:
a primitive root;
to tumble, i.e. be violently agitated; specifically, to crash (of thunder); figuratively, to irritate (with anger)
KJV: make to fret, roar, thunder, trouble.

H7482.definition:
from H7481 (רָעַם);
a peal of thunder
KJV: thunder.

H7483.definition:
feminine of H7482 (רַעַם);
the mane of a horse (as quivering in the wind)
KJV: thunder.

H7484.definition:
the same as H7483 (רַעְמָה);
Ramah, the name of a grandson of Ham, and of a place (perhaps founded by him)
KJV: Raamah.

H7485.definition:
from H7481 (רָעַם) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has shaken;
Raamjah, an Israelite
KJV: Raamiah.

H7486.definition:
or רַעַמְסֵס; of Egyptian origin;
Rameses or Raamses, a place in Egypt
KJV: Raamses, Rameses.

H7487.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7488 (רַעֲנָן);
green, i.e. (figuratively) prosperous
KJV: flourishing.

H7488.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be green;
verdant; by analogy, new; figuratively, prosperous
KJV: green, flourishing.

H7489.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to spoil (literally, by breaking to pieces); figuratively, to make (or be) good fornothing, i.e. bad (physically, socially or morally)
KJV: afflict, associate selves (by mistake for H7462 (רָעָה)), break (down, in pieces), [phrase] displease, (be, bring, do) evil (doer, entreat, man), show self friendly (by mistake for H7462 (רָעָה)), do harm, (do) hurt, (behave self, deal) ill, [idiom] indeed, do mischief, punish, still, vex, (do) wicked (doer, -ly), be (deal, do) worse.

H7490.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7489 (רָעַע)
{properly, to spoil (literally, by breaking to pieces); figuratively, to make (or be) good fornothing, i.e. bad (physically, socially or morally)}
KJV: break, bruise.

H7491.definition:
a primitive root;
to drip
KJV: distil, drop (down).

H7492.definition:
a primitive root;
to break in pieces; figuratively, harass
KJV: dash in pieces, vex.

H7493.definition:
a primitive root;
to undulate (as the earth, the sky, etc.; also a field of grain), particularly through fear; specifically, to spring (as a locust)
KJV: make afraid, (re-) move, quake, (make to) shake, (make to) tremble.

H7494.definition:
from H7493 (רָעַשׁ);
vibration, bounding, uproar
KJV: commotion, confused noise, earthquake, fierceness, quaking, rattling, rushing, shaking.

H7495.definition:
or רָפָה; a primitive root;
properly, to mend (by stitching), i.e. (figuratively) to cure
KJV: cure, (cause to) heal, physician, repair, [idiom] thoroughly, make whole. See H7503 (רָפָה).

H7496.definition:
from H7495 (רָפָא) in the sense of H7503 (רָפָה);
properly, lax, i.e. (figuratively) a ghost (as dead; in plural only)
KJV: dead, deceased.

H7497.definition:
or רָפָה; from H7495 (רָפָא) in the sense of invigorating;
a giant
KJV: giant, Rapha, Rephaim(-s). See also H1051 (בֵּית רָפָא).

H7498.definition:
or רָפָה; probably the same as H7497 (רָפָא); giant;
Rapha or Raphah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Rapha.

H7499.definition:
feminine passive participle of H7495 (רָפָא);
a medicament
KJV: heal(-ed), medicine.
